@quotation
@strong{@anchor{Exercise 4.33}Exercise 4.33:} Ben Bitdiddle tests the lazy list
implementation given above by evaluating the expression

@example typescript
readAll("head([1, 2, 3]);")
@end example

To his surprise, this produces an error.  After some thought, he realizes that
the ``lists'' built from array literals are ordinary eager arrays, different
from the lazy lists manipulated by the new definitions of @code{pair},
@code{head}, and @code{tail}.  Modify the lazy experiments' treatment of array
and object literals so that
list data typed at the driver loop will produce true lazy lists.
@end quotation

